TFConstants troop IDs are used throughout army operations:

```actionscript
// Building troops
barracks.train(TFConstants.T_ARCHER, 100);

// Army composition
army.setTroops(TFConstants.T_CAVALRY, 500);

// Battle calculations
if (troopType == TFConstants.T_CATAPHRACT) {
    // Heavy cavalry bonus
}
```

Note: Always check ID ranges (2-13 for troops, 20-25 for forts).

Error handling best practices:

```actionscript
switch (response.errorCode) {
    case ErrorCode.RESOURCE_NOT_ENOUGH:
        // Check which resource
        break;
    case ErrorCode.NO_DEPEND_BUILDING:
        showBuildingRequirements();
        break;
    case ErrorCode.ALLIANCE_NOT_FOUND:
        // BUG: Also matches SUPPORT_NOT_ZERO!
        // Needs context to differentiate
        break;
    default:
        log("Unknown error: " + response.errorCode);
}
```

Note: Always handle the -52 duplicate case by checking context.
